{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791143412,"nonce":"wGJy4C1aPopDnxhxonFdfluvY3E=","title":"the native pump does not tell the runtime it is blocking","message":"Requested by ash-fd for ashui's memory work (ash git-bug 9e5b224). Ash's idle collector runs once every Haxe thread has spent 300 ms inside a native call marked blocking (hl_blocking). ashui's UI thread waits in xwindow's pump_app_events, which doesn't mark itself, so Ash can't collect while the UI is idle, and its ordinary collections stall on that thread.\n\nWrap the pump in the runtime's blocking convention. Inside the pump the backend only queues events in Rust's memory: Text is Arc\u003cstr\u003e, conversion to runtime values happens after the call returns, and host::raise is called only from entry points. So the whole pumped pump_app_events can be marked blocking.\n\nUnder a host (Drive::Turns, iOS) the program's turn runs inside winit's loop, so that path would need blocking switched off around the turn. Not done, since Ash doesn't drive a hosted loop yet.","files":null}]}